/-!
# Candidate-specification studies and their evidence

This is a queryable index, not the definition of a selected language. Each
decision has a normative question, actual theorem terms, separately recorded
selection state, and remaining investigations. Requirement descriptions and
suggested experiments are metadata, not formalized necessity claims.

`DesignStudy.Specification` is the independent formal interface for turning a
question into a study over a stated candidate class. Its evidence is indexed
by one candidate; its completion theorem cannot assemble unrelated models.
The finite evaluation study already exercises that interface. The records
below also connect existing, substantially richer calculus results without
pretending that all six questions have one jointly qualified answer.

Runtime observations are deliberately absent here. `PrimeComparisons` joins
this index to separately pinned CeTTa observations and bounded model evidence.
-/

